<para>This test requires the split boundaries to be partly seperating four Regions (bottom left, bottom right, Top left, Top right) for it to work</para>
<para>0) Tests nodes are matching when using Interface::MatchingN(i,side) 1) <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_test" kindref="compound">Test</ref> Unit normals 2) <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_test" kindref="compound">Test</ref> Inside nodes of Interface match exactly with the face of the Inner Parent nodes (and not slightly rotated, which is not good enough). 3) Tests all OUTSIDE elements parents have the CORRECT new nodes on OUTSIDE, including elements that do not share a face with the interface </para>
